# Medora — Admin Integration Session Record

| | |
|---|---|
| **Date** | 30 October 2026 |
| **Repository** | `C:\Graduation Project\med` |
| **Branch** | `main` |
| **Database** | `medora_db` (PostgreSQL 18), migrations `001`–`005` |
| **Scope** | Admin **Users** and **Doctors & Staff**, backend + the minimum frontend data layer |
| **Status** | Implemented and verified; dev stack running on `:3000` + `:5000` |

---

## 1. Executive summary

The session began as a request to complete the admin dashboard backend and ended with both admin
pages reading PostgreSQL, the account lifecycle working end to end, and two sign-in defects found
and fixed.

What changed:

1. **Schema** — migrations `004` and `005` added the workforce and account-lifecycle layer the two
   pages need. The documented staging plan was renumbered to make room.
2. **Backend** — 11 admin endpoints plus a public activation endpoint, with role + permission +
   CSRF enforcement, atomic provisioning, status transitions, invitations, audit and security
   events.
3. **Frontend** — the mock providers were replaced with API calls; hardcoded specialty, department
   and location lists now come from the database; status, invitation and verification actions were
   wired.
4. **Tooling** — an opt-in demo seed script that goes through the real provisioning service.
5. **Defects fixed** — doctors were bounced back to `/login` by a role-routing bug; a CORS
   allowlist rejected the `:3001` dev origin and surfaced as a generic 500.

Nothing is seeded automatically. `medora_db` contains only accounts that were actually created.

---

## 2. Starting point (verified before any change)

| Area | State at the start |
|---|---|
| Backend | Express 5.3, `pg` 8.23, session cookie `medora_session`, Argon2id, CSRF on logout only |
| Mounted routes | `/api/auth` plus two demo checks; no admin module |
| RBAC | `requireAuth`, `requireRole`, `requirePermission` existed — the last one was unused |
| Database | Migrations `001`–`003`, 10 tables, 1 admin, 12 specialties, 0 doctors, 0 staff |
| Frontend | `/admin/users` and `/admin/doctors-staff` fed by `seedUsers` and `mergeMembers(users)`; no fetch calls |
| Schema docs | `medora.dbml` with **45 tables** (10 implemented, 35 proposed), 129 relationships, 8 table groups |

The decisive constraint: **the pages could not read the database without a frontend change.**
There is no backend-only mechanism that pushes rows into a client component's state.

---

## 3. Schema review and the corrections it forced

Revision 1 of the plan had been written from the identity/profile section plus keyword searches. A
full read of the ERD invalidated parts of it:

| # | Earlier assumption | Reality | Consequence |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Use `004`/`005` for admin | `SCHEMA_ARCHITECTURE.md` §11 already assigned `004` to scheduling and `005` to consultation capture; the runner rejects duplicate version prefixes | Staging renumbered before any SQL was written |
| 2 | Build a minimal audit table | `audit_logs`, `security_events`, `notifications` were already fully designed | Implemented exactly as designed |
| 3 | No FK on `audit_logs.actor_user_id` | The canonical relationship list defines it as `ON DELETE SET NULL` | FK added |
| 4 | No source for duty/availability | `doctor_availability`, `doctor_time_off`, `appointments` are designed | Dropped the proposed `duty_status` column; those fields stay empty until scheduling exists |
| 5 | Add a `departments` table silently | `specialties` was designated as the Departments table | Made an explicit decision and documented the revision |
| 6 | Add `photo_url` | No avatar column anywhere; storage is an open decision | Deferred; the UI uses initials |
| 7 | Name it `account_invitations` | Open decision #14 names it `user_invitations` | Renamed |

Confirmed genuine gaps across all 45 tables: **no staff/employment profile, no doctor DOB/years/
location, no non-clinical organizational unit, no invitation table, no avatar column.**

---

## 4. Decisions (all resolved)

| # | Decision | Chosen | Result |
|---|---|---|---|
| D-1 | Frontend wiring | **(b)** non-visual data-layer change | Pages read the API; no layout redesign |
| D-2 | Migration sequencing | **(a)** renumber, admin first | `004`–`005` admin; old `004`–`013` shifted to `006`–`014` |
| D-3 | Department model | **(a)** new `departments` table | Clinical rows 1:1 with specialties; support rows separate |
| D-4 | Demo data | **Added, opt-in** | `seed-demo-workforce.js`; never automatic; `medora_db` not seeded |

