## 5. Database changes

### 5.1 Migration `004_admin_workforce.sql`

| Object | Detail |
|---|---|
| `clinic_locations` | `UNIQUE (name, city)`, `country_code`, `timezone`; seeded with Main Hospital, West Clinic, Children's Clinic |
| `departments` | `kind ∈ {clinical, support}`; clinical rows carry a unique `specialty_id`; CHECK enforces the two shapes; 12 clinical + 3 support seeded |
| `staff_profiles` | 1:1 with `users` (CASCADE), `department_id` RESTRICT, job title, employment id (partial unique), phone, DOB, bio, work shift, location |
| `doctor_profiles` | Added `date_of_birth`, `years_of_experience`, `primary_location_id`, `verification_status`; CHECKs for DOB floor, 0–70 years, three verification states, and "verified requires a timestamp" |
| `users` | Added `trg_users_updated_at` — the column existed since `001` with nothing maintaining it |
| Guard | `prevent_department_delete()` blocks deleting a clinical department while doctors reference its specialty (`Admin.md` §6.4) |

### 5.2 Migration `005_admin_account_lifecycle.sql`

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `user_invitations` | SHA-256 token hash, `purpose ∈ {invite, password_reset}`, expiry, single use, one live invite per user (partial unique index) |
| `notifications` | Delivery record; category/channel/status CHECKs; never carries tokens |
| `audit_logs` | Append-only; actor `SET NULL`, never cascaded; redacted before/after state |
| `security_events` | Authentication, session, rate-limit, CSRF and `privilege_changed` events |

### 5.3 Staging renumbering

| New | Old | File |
|---|---|---|
| 004 | new | `004_admin_workforce.sql` |
| 005 | new | `005_admin_account_lifecycle.sql` |
| 006 | 004 | scheduling and care access |
| 007 | 005 | consultation capture |
| 008 | 006 | AI execution envelope |
| 009 | 007 | transcripts and approvals |
| 010 | 008 | reports and delivery |
| 011 | 009 | medical records and Agent 2 |
| 012 | 010 | follow-ups and proposals |
| 013 | 011 | reference knowledge |
| 014 | 013 | constraints, seeds, hardening |
| — | 012 | absorbed into `005` |

Documentation updated in the same change: `medora.dbml` (48 tables, 136 relationships, validated
with `dbml2sql`), `SCHEMA_ARCHITECTURE.md` (§1.3, §10, §11, §12, §13, §14, §15),
`SCHEMA_DATA_DICTIONARY.md` (§2, §10).

