## 6. Backend implementation

### 6.1 Endpoints

| Method | Path | Permission |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/admin/users` | `users.manage` **or** `staff_accounts.view` |
| GET | `/api/admin/users/:id` | same |
| POST | `/api/admin/users` | `staff_accounts.create` |
| PATCH | `/api/admin/users/:id` | `staff_accounts.update` |
| PATCH | `/api/admin/users/:id/status` | `staff_accounts.disable` |
| POST | `/api/admin/users/:id/invitations` | `staff_accounts.invite` |
| GET | `/api/admin/doctors-staff` | `staff_accounts.view` |
| GET | `/api/admin/doctors-staff/:id` | `staff_accounts.view` |
| PATCH | `/api/admin/doctors-staff/:id` | `staff_accounts.update` |
| POST | `/api/admin/doctors-staff/:id/verification` | `staff_accounts.update` |
| GET | `/api/admin/reference-data` | `staff_accounts.view` |
| POST | `/api/auth/activate` | public, rate-limited |

Every admin route is `requireAuth` → `requireRole("admin")` → specific permission → `verifyCsrf`
on mutations. `requireAnyPermission` was added because the existing helper requires **all** listed
permissions.

### 6.2 Vocabulary mapping

| `users.status` | API / UI |
|---|---|
| `active` | `active` |
| `pending_activation` | `pending` |
| `suspended` | `suspended` |
| `disabled` | `inactive` |

| DB role | API role |
|---|---|
| `doctor` | `doctor` |
| `receptionist` | `staff` |
| `patient` | `patient` |
| `admin` | excluded from these endpoints |

Primary role precedence: `doctor` > `receptionist` > `patient`. Accounts whose only role is
`admin` never appear in the list, stats or mutation targets.

### 6.3 Provisioning transaction

One transaction: duplicate-email check → `users` (`pending_activation`, `password_hash NULL`,
`created_by`) → `user_roles` → doctor or staff profile → `user_invitations` → `notifications` →
`audit_logs` → commit. A failure at any step leaves zero orphan rows.

The admin never chooses or sees a password. The API returns a one-time activation link, which the
UI shows once with a copy button.

### 6.4 Status lifecycle

| From → To | Allowed | Note |
|---|---|---|
| `active` → `suspended` / `disabled` | yes | reason required |
| `suspended` → `active` / `disabled` | yes | reason required |
| `disabled` → `active` | yes | 409 if no password |
| `pending_activation` → `disabled` | yes | revokes the live invitation |
| `pending_activation` → `active` | no | only `/api/auth/activate` |
| any → same | no | 409 `status_unchanged` |
| target is self | no | 403 `self_lockout` |
| target holds `admin` | no | 403 `admin_protected` |

Every change writes an `audit_logs` row (with the reason) and a `security_events`
`privilege_changed` row.

### 6.5 Invitations

- Tokens are 32 random bytes, stored only as SHA-256 hashes.
- Invite TTL 7 days; password-reset TTL 24 hours.
- Issuing a new token revokes the previous live one.
- Activation: `invite` sets `status = active`; `password_reset` keeps the current status and
  revokes all existing sessions.
- Rate-limited; password policy identical to registration.

### 6.6 Errors

`errorHandler` now passes through `err.code`, so clients get stable codes:
`validation_error`, `email_taken`, `license_taken`, `employment_id_taken`, `unknown_specialty`,
`unknown_department`, `unknown_location`, `department_specialty_mismatch`,
`invalid_status_transition`, `status_unchanged`, `pending_activation_incomplete`,
`self_lockout`, `admin_protected`, `not_found`, `token_invalid`, `token_expired`,
`invitation_not_applicable`, `cors_origin_denied`.

