## 8. Demo seed (D-4)

`Backend/scripts/seed-demo-workforce.js`, exposed as `npm run db:seed:demo`.

- 7 doctors + 5 staff, `@medora.example` addresses, created through `adminUsersService.provisionUser`.
- Requires `--confirm`; refuses `NODE_ENV=production`; refuses non-local hosts unless
  `--allow-remote`; skips existing emails; aborts without an admin actor.
- `--activate` sets a generated password per account and prints credentials once; `--links` prints
  activation links instead.
- Verified on `medora_test`: 12 created / 0 failed; re-run 0 created / 12 skipped; both guards
  refused. `medora_db` was not seeded.

---

## 9. Defects found and fixed

### 9.1 Doctor sign-in bounced to `/login`

`LoginPage` sent every non-admin to `/patient/dashboard`; the patient guard rejected the doctor
role and redirected to `/login`. The session was valid throughout.

Fix: `role-home.ts` mapping used by both `LoginPage` and `RouteGuard`; `/workspace` added as the
doctor/staff destination; unknown roles now get an explicit message instead of a redirect loop.

### 9.2 "An unexpected error occurred" on sign-in

Next had fallen back to `:3001` (3000 was busy), so the browser origin was
`http://localhost:3001`. The backend allowlist contained only `:3000`, and the CORS callback raised
a plain `Error`, which the handler rendered as a 500.

Fix: development accepts any loopback origin on any port; a denied origin returns
`403 cors_origin_denied` and logs `[CORS] Blocked origin`. Production keeps the explicit list.

### 9.3 Two dev servers sharing `.next`

Two `next dev` instances wrote the same cache, producing 404s for hashed chunks. Consolidated to a
single stack on `:3000` + `:5000`; the cache was moved out of the project (the sandbox blocks bulk
deletion).

### 9.4 Smaller corrections

- Work location was free text and failed validation unless typed exactly; now a database select.
- The creation dialog still said "Demo only — no database record"; corrected.
- Invitation notes promised an email that is never sent; corrected.
- The activity tab claimed audit logging was unimplemented; corrected.

